# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets — .assetsignore (gitignore syntax, relative to the assets dir = dist)
# Purpose: keep the static-asset upload under Cloudflare's 20,000-file limit WITHOUT breaking visible images.
#
# Strategy (no R2 yet): deploy every HERO image and exclude ONLY the hotel GALLERY extras (-2/-3/-4/-5).
#   - Kept (served as static /images/): heroes/, cities/, images/cm/ (3,216 — hub Editor's Picks + per-area
#     "where to stay" cards + attraction articles), images/food/, images/gallery/, AND images/hotels/*-1.jpg
#     (1,650 hotel hero shots used by hub hotel cards + top10 roundups + each review's main photo) + ~472
#     non-standard-named hotel files.
#   - Excluded (only place they appear is the gallery strip on individual hotel-review pages, which all use
#     onerror="this.style.opacity='0'" so they hide gracefully): images/hotels/*-2..-5.jpg (≈5,571 files).
# File count: 22,627 total − 5,571 gallery extras ≈ 17,056 static files → under 20,000. ✓
#
# FULL FIX (serve gallery extras too): upload astro/public/images/hotels to an R2 bucket, set PUBLIC_IMG_BASE
# to its public URL (ReviewLayout already routes hotel images through asset()/PUBLIC_IMG_BASE), then exclude
# all of images/hotels/ here. See _internal/assetsignore.for-cutover for the full R2 cutover.
images/hotels/*-2.jpg
images/hotels/*-3.jpg
images/hotels/*-4.jpg
images/hotels/*-5.jpg
